{"schema_version":1,"task_id":"theory-e0b9594db89f8da6","paper_id":"2505.16284v1","variant":"original","kind":"theory","outcome":"checked","reason":null,"error":null,"findings":[{"finding_id":"theory-e0b9594db89f8da6-f0","task_id":"theory-e0b9594db89f8da6","paper_id":"2505.16284v1","variant":"original","error_class":"math_error","anchor":{"kind":"sentence","sentence_id":"s145","start":0,"end":45},"target":{"kind":"setting","key":"math"},"summary":"Lemma 5.1: The paper defines the infinity norm of a matrix A as A_\nu := \text{max}_{j,l} |A_{j,l}| (the maximum absolute entry) in sentence [s92]. In Fact 3.3 [s101] and Lemma 5.1 [s145], the paper assumes submultiplicativity of the form AB_\nu ≤ A_\nu B_\nu. However, for the max-entry norm, matrix multiplication is not submultiplicative without a dimension factor; multiplying two d × d matrices of al","explanation":"high confidence. The paper defines the infinity norm of a matrix A as A_\nu := \text{max}_{j,l} |A_{j,l}| (the maximum absolute entry) in sentence [s92]. In Fact 3.3 [s101] and Lemma 5.1 [s145], the paper assumes submultiplicativity of the form AB_\nu ≤ A_\nu B_\nu. However, for the max-entry norm, matrix multiplication is not submultiplicative without a dimension factor; multiplying two d × d matrices of all ones yields an entry-wise maximum of d rather than 1. Consequently, Lemma 5.1's bound K := (e^\theta - 1) W_v \nu fails to account for the dimension d accumulated during matrix multiplications (such as X W_v), making the claimed bound Res(SAtt(X))_\nu ≤ K • Res(X)_\nu mathematically incorrect unless scaled by d (or unless the norm is defined as the induced ℓ_− ∑ norm). Witness: K := d • (e^\theta - 1) • W_v \nu (incorporating the hidden dimension d required due to the failure of submultiplicativity for max-entry norms).","evidence":[{"kind":"quote","source":{"kind":"submission","id":"2505.16284v1","title":null,"url":null},"text":"Then, we have Res(SAtt(X)) ∞ ≤ K • Res(X) ∞ .","page":null,"char_start":0,"char_end":45,"path":null,"line_start":null,"line_end":null}],"uncertain":false}],"attempts":1}
